{"slug": "instrument-io-list-dcs-plc", "targets": ["plc io list"], "html": "<h2 style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:700;color:#0186e0;margin:34px 0 16px;\">PLC IO List Example With Typical Rows</h2><p>A <strong>PLC IO list</strong> is the same signal register used for a DCS, written for a PLC rack, slot and channel layout. Each row is one signal, so a single valve with a positioner and two limit switches takes three rows. The sample rows below show how AI, AO, DI and DO signals are typically entered.</p><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:16px;\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Tag</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Description</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Type</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Signal / range</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Rack / slot / channel</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">PT 101</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Pump discharge pressure</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">AI</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">4 to 20 mA, 0 to 10 bar</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0 / 3 / 0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">FCV 102</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Flow control valve output</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">AO</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">4 to 20 mA, 0 to 100 %</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0 / 5 / 0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">ZSO 102</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Valve open limit switch</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">DI</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">24 V DC dry contact</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0 / 7 / 4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">ZSC 102</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Valve closed limit switch</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">DI</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">24 V DC dry contact</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0 / 7 / 5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">P 101 RUN</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Pump running feedback</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">DI</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">24 V DC from MCC</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0 / 7 / 6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">P 101 START</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Pump start command</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">DO</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Relay output to MCC</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">0 / 9 / 0</td></tr></table></div><p>Steps to turn the list into hardware:</p><ol><li>Group the rows by signal type and by intrinsically safe or non IS.</li><li>Count channels of each type and add the project spare percentage.</li><li>Divide by channels per card and round up to get the card count.</li><li>Assign rack, slot and channel, then issue the list to the panel builder.</li></ol>"}